# Copy to .env to change development. Nothing here is required: every value has a default in
# compose.yaml or compose.override.yaml. .env is gitignored — keys stay on your machine.

# ── The model ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The model runs in the browser, on WebGPU, and the browser downloads it once (about 2.3 GB) from
# keasy's own origin, never a third party's: `make models` fetches it — the MLC weights from Hugging
# Face and the compiled library from WebLLM's releases, both pinned in infra/models.sh and checked —
# into KEASY_MODELS with app-config.json, the listing the page reads, and the stack's `models` service
# serves that directory at /models. With no listing there is no model, and Ask and the assistant say so.
# KEASY_MODELS=./infra/models

# ── The platform ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The kanzo-ui release the identity service comes from; the default is the one compose.override.yaml names.
# KANZO_UI_REF=
